                <pb facs="0762" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/454: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Goold</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-21T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>17. Legation’s despatch No. 3, March 1, 1919.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d608-f1"/>
                    Advice and consent of the Senate to the ratification of the Treaty as amended by
                    agreement with Colombian Government was given yesterday without further
                    amendments. Vote was 69 to 19. Inform Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
